# Action Button Icons

Apply to every **Add**, **Edit**, **Delete**, and **View** control in the web UI (tables, toolbars, dialogs, cards, etc.).

## Rules

1. **Add** — Always represented with a **plus** icon (not text-only “Add” as the sole affordance). Label text may accompany the icon when helpful (e.g. “Add”), but the plus icon is required.

2. **Edit** — Always represented with a **pencil** icon (not text-only “Edit” as the sole affordance). Optional accompanying label is fine.

3. **Delete** — Always represented with a **trash** icon in **red** (use the project danger/red token, e.g. `text-danger`). Do not use a neutral-colored trash icon for delete.

4. **View** — Always represented with an **eye** icon (not text-only “View” as the sole affordance). Optional accompanying label is fine.

5. **Close** — Always represented with an **X (cross)** icon (not text-only “Close” as the sole affordance). Optional accompanying label is fine. Icon-only Close needs `aria-label="Close"`.

6. **Dialog Close placement** — Every dialog (including confirm/alert dialogs) must have a Close (X) control in the **top-right corner**. Do not place Close beside the primary footer action (Apply, Delete, Save, etc.). The footer holds the main action only. Prefer shared `DetailDialog` so this chrome is automatic.

## Guidance

- Prefer shared icon components under `components/shared/` when extracting reusable icons (`CloseButton`, `AddButton`, etc.).
- Icon-only buttons must have an accessible `aria-label` (e.g. `Add`, `Edit`, `Delete`, `View`, `Close`).
- Confirm dialogs for delete may keep a text **Delete** confirm button; the trigger that opens delete must still use the red trash icon. Dismiss/close is the top-right X (not a footer Close/Cancel beside Delete).

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — text-only row actions
<button type="button">Edit</button>
<button type="button">Delete</button>

// ✅ GOOD — icon affordances
<button type="button" aria-label="Add">/* plus icon */</button>
<button type="button" aria-label="Edit">/* pencil icon */</button>
<button type="button" aria-label="Close">/* X cross icon */</button>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Close beside the main action
<div className="flex justify-end gap-2">
  <CloseButton onClick={onClose} />
  <button type="button">Apply</button>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — Close in the dialog header; footer is the main action
<div className="flex items-start justify-between">
  <h2>Add metadata</h2>
  <CloseButton onClick={onClose} />
</div>
<div className="flex justify-end">
  <button type="button">Apply</button>
</div>
```
